-- pending: U2 and SPEC §27 (a finaliser that performs an operation, run when a task holding a lend is cancelled)
-- now: 41:10: unknown variable `await`
-- Hard problem 9: a task lends a buffer it owns, holds the view across its `await`, and guards the
-- `await` with a finaliser. When `main` cancels the task, the finaliser runs with the lend still
-- open: it reads and overwrites the buffer through the view, and reports the value it saw by
-- performing `note`, an operation of the `Audit` handler around the whole run. Then the lend
-- ends and the buffer is freed.
--
-- Issue: SPEC §27 (finalisers with effects) and docs/async-capabilities.md A6 (a finaliser that
-- logs); U2 (the surface has no finaliser form); #682 (the lend held across the `await`). The
-- finaliser here is the body's `[then]`, which SPEC §27 types at its own row and lets perform
-- operations; R1's `· ⊢ d : Ref T ⊸ 1` is the lend's own finaliser, a different one. The core-text
-- form is `corpus/pending/hard-async-cancel-finaliser-op-core.bc`, refused because the core text
-- cannot write the cancel row that would carry `note`. `corpus/async-cancel.bc` cancels a task
-- holding a lend with no finaliser of its own.
--
-- Rust: a guard whose `Drop` holds the `&mut` and writes through it when the future is dropped; a
-- `Drop` cannot `.await` (async drop is unstable), so an operation it performs must be synchronous.
--
-- Spelling (a hypothesis): the core text's `x <- M unwind (D); N` written in a surface body.
--
-- Today: refused before the borrow is reached. The surface has no finaliser form, and the core's
-- binding form `x <- M unwind (D)` takes a core computation, so `await()` is an unknown variable
-- there. All three stages (`bcc check`, `bcc run --backend old`, `--backend new`) stop there.
--
-- Once it lands: i32[110]: `note(1)` before the `await`, then the finaliser's `note(10)`, the value
-- it read through the view; `live 0` (the buffer freed after the lend ends).

include async

effect Audit { fn note(x: i32) }

handler audit(mut seen: i32): Audit = {
  note(x) = { seen = seen * 100 + x; () }
}

fn victim() -> i32 with Async, Audit =
  let buf = alloc(10);
  let v = borrow mut buf { m ->
    note(1);
    u <- await() unwind (note(modify m { x -> (99, x) }));
    modify m { x -> (x + 1, x) }
  };
  let _ = free(buf);
  v

main -> i32 =
  let log = alloc(0);
  let u = with audit(&mut log) {
    let t = with spawn { victim() };
    cancel(t)
  };
  free(log)
